Here's a feature that I'd like to see added to hack.  When you try to move
into a square occupied by a monster, the default is to attack with your weapon,
or fists if you have no weapon.  I'd like to see a way of specifying the kind
of attack you do, as opposed to the default to a weapon attack.  For example,
priests kick REALLY well, so a priest's default attack could be set to kicking
(in the direction of the monster).  A tourist can't fight very well, but has
nice darts, so his default attack could be set to 'throw a (darts)' (in the
direction of the monster).  This isn't something that would be for each class.
Anyone could set their attack to any action.  For example, a samurai black
dragon may want to set his attack to #monster.  Someone with 99 potions of
sickness may want to set it to 'throw d (potion)'.  Someone who was being
completely pacifistic could set the attack to #chat.  That's basically the
idea.  

What does everyone else think?  
